From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Komh <mail@guojing.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:37:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cli: add flatpak clean command

Removes what flatpak keeps around but never uses again:

- extra-data embedded in commits (see "deploy: discard embedded extra
  data after use"), for installations from before that change;
- interrupted extra-data prefetches and .part files;
- empty directories that deleted refs and remotes leave in repo/refs,
  checkouts of interrupted deployments, partial-commit markers of
  commits that are gone, and -origin remotes of uninstalled bundles.

The data of apps that are no longer installed (~/.var/app, overrides,
portal permissions) is listed, and only deleted with --delete-data.

Like other commands it covers the user and system installations by
default; a system installation that is not writable is only inspected,
with a hint to run it as root. Writable repositories are cleaned under
the exclusive locks prune takes. --dry-run reports without changing
anything.
